        <h2 style="color: var(--cream);">Crystal Tubbs</h2>
        <p>
          Crystal Tubbs is a researcher, builder, and systems thinker whose work centers on reliable AI,
          experimental design, interpretability, and applied innovation. Her research connects technical inquiry
          with practical, human centered system design.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Focus areas include LLM reliability, stabilization, evaluation design, and emerging intelligent systems.</li>
          <li>Research spans architectural behavior, structured experimentation, and trustworthy AI workflows.</li>
          <li>Connected initiatives include CIPHER, PRISM, SAF, Chrysalis, and dashboard driven evaluation environments.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <article class="card bio">
        <div class="tag">About me</div>
        <h2>Research grounded in structure, transformation, and dependable intelligence</h2>
        <p>
          My work explores how advanced AI systems can become more reliable, interpretable, and practically useful.
          Through experiments, frameworks, and linked research initiatives, I investigate how architecture,
          evaluation, and design choices shape system behavior.
        </p>
        <p>
          In addition to the architectural stabilization of LLMs project, my research portfolio includes CIPHER,
          PRISM, and SAF, as well as the broader Chrysalis initiative. Together, these efforts reflect a strong
          interest in structured intelligence, resilient systems, and meaningful transformation in AI research.
        </p>
        <p>
